\frac{(9-K_P)(1+K_P)}{8}\] To find the maximum possible value of \(K_I\), define \[f(K_P)=\frac{(9-K_P)(1+K_P)}{8}\] \[f(K_P)=\frac{9+8K_P-K_P^2}{8}\] Maximum value occurs when \[\frac{df}{dK_P}=0\] \[\frac{1}{8}(8-2K_P)=0\] \[8-2K_P=0\] \[K_P=4\] Substituting \(K_P=4\), \[K_I&lt;
